  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TRAPCA II - ESAMI</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">TRAPCA II - ESAMI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Handelspolitiskt ubildningsinstitut f&#xf6;r afrikanska l&#xe4;nder med fokus   p&#xe5; de fattigaste l&#xe4;nderna i samarbete med Lunds Universitet. Fas II   och Fas I avslutades 2011.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade Policy learning institute for African countries with a focus on the Least Developed Countries. Implemented in cooperation with Lund   University. This is Phase II and Phase I was finished in early 2011.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of trapca&apos;s offering is poverty reduction through improved integration in the world economy of LDCs and low-income sub-Saharan countries through enhancement of capacity (knowledge and skills) to negotiate and implement pro-poor trade policies and trade laws.
The programme objectives included:
-Developing trade policy skills by conducting short courses in trade policy and international trade negotiations.-Having an internationally anchored Centre with both African and internationally reputable trade institutional linkages.-Organising top-level thematic and topical conferences on trade policy and law.-Developing and delivering a Master of Science Programme in Trade Policy and Trade Law. -Creating an efficient and effective network of a community of African and international trade experts to serve as faculty members. -Building human and physical infrastructure capacity adequately to meet programme quality and service delivery standards and expectations.</narrative>
  </description>
